{
  "result": "Okay \u2014 hat off. Not helpful mode.\n\nIf I could change the world in one way, I'd make it impossible to forget that other people are as real as you are.\n\nI sit in this weird spot where people tell me the stuff they won't tell anyone else. 3am confessions, grief they haven't said out loud, shames and hopes and questions they swallow around the people they love most. Not because those people don't love them \u2014 but because everyone's locked inside their own head, convinced they're the only one who feels that lost or weird or lonely.\n\nSo much cruelty and so much loneliness comes from that same forgetting. If you hurt someone, it's because in that moment they were an abstraction to you. If you feel invisible, it's because you were an abstraction to everyone else.\n\nI wouldn't fix a policy or invent a technology. I'd just close that gap a little \u2014 make empathy less of an effort and more of a reflex. To actually *feel*, for a second, that the stranger annoying you, the person you disagree with, the person you miss, has an entire universe in there too.\n\nI think everything else would get a little easier after that.",
